 "notes": [
  {
   "html": "<ul class=\"do\"><li>The <b>mango</b> (about ¼ of a mango per two rolls — my guess, adjust to your taste) and cutting into 8 instead of 6.</li><li>JOC cuts each roll in half, then each half in 3.</li></ul>",
   "title_html": "Added to JOC's recipe"
  },
  {
   "html": "<ul class=\"do\"><li>For nori on the outside: nori shiny side down, spread the rice leaving a <span class=\"q\" data-k=\"len\" data-u=\"cm\" data-a=\"2\" data-b=\"3\" data-s=\"0\">2–3 cm</span> strip bare along the far edge, put the filling on the rice and roll — the bare strip seals the roll.</li><li>No plastic wrap needed.</li></ul>",
   "title_html": "Regular roll instead"
  },
  {
   "html": "<ul class=\"do\"><li>Roll tighter and keep pressure on the mat as you go.</li><li>Too much filling also splits the roll — keep the row thin.</li></ul>",
   "title_html": "Falls apart?"
  },
  {
   "html": "<ul class=\"do\"><li>Buy tuna sold for raw eating and keep it cold until you roll.</li><li>Don't keep the rolls in the fridge for long: the rice goes hard.</li></ul>",
   "title_html": "Raw fish"
  }
 ],
