    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "body_html": "<ul class=\"do\"><li>Turn the sheet over so the rice is face down on the plastic.</li><li>Line the nori up with the near edge of the mat.</li></ul>",
   "heat": null,
   "id": "step-6",
   "images": {
    "alt": "Flip it",
    "diagram": null,
    "how": [
     {
      "caption": "Flip it so the rice faces down; line the nori up with the near edge.",
      "src": "illustrations/tuna-mango-roll/6-how1.webp"
     }
    ],
    "illustration": null,
    "photo": null,
    "result": "illustrations/tuna-mango-roll/6.webp",
    "svg_fallback": null
   },
   "n": 6,
   "part": null,
   "part_id": null,
   "time": "10 s",
   "time_html": "<span>10 s</span>",
   "title": "Flip it",
   "uses_rows": []
  },
  {
   "body_html": "<p>Lay half the tuna mixture in a thin row along the near edge of the nori, with a strip of mango right next to it.</p>",
   "heat": null,
   "id": "step-7",
   "images": {
    "alt": "Filling along the near edge",
    "diagram": null,
    "how": [
     {
      "caption": "Tuna in a thin row along the near edge, mango right beside it.",
      "src": "illustrations/tuna-mango-roll/7-how1.webp"
     }
    ],
    "illustration": null,
    "photo": null,
    "result": "illustrations/tuna-mango-roll/7.webp",
    "svg_fallback": null
   },
   "n": 7,
   "part": null,
   "part_id": null,
   "time": "1 min",
   "time_html": "<span>1 min</span>",
   "title": "Filling along the near edge",
   "uses_rows": []
  },
  {
   "body_html": "<ul class=\"do\"><li>Hold the filling in place with your fingers.</li><li>Lift the near edge of the mat with your thumbs and roll the nori quickly and tightly over the filling.</li><li>Tuck the edge in, then pull the far end of the mat towards you to keep gentle pressure.</li></ul>",
   "heat": null,
   "id": "step-8",
   "images": {
    "alt": "Lift and tuck",
    "diagram": null,
    "how": [
     {
      "caption": "Fingers hold the filling; thumbs lift the near edge of the mat.",
      "src": "illustrations/tuna-mango-roll/8-how1.webp"
     },
     {
      "caption": "Roll over the filling and tuck the edge in tight.",
      "src": "illustrations/tuna-mango-roll/8-how2.webp"
     }
    ],
    "illustration": null,
    "photo": null,
    "result": "illustrations/tuna-mango-roll/8.webp",
    "svg_fallback": null
   },
   "n": 8,
   "part": null,
   "part_id": null,
   "time": "20 s",
   "time_html": "<span>20 s</span>",
   "title": "Lift and tuck",
   "uses_rows": []
  },
  {
   "body_html": "<p>Lift the edge of the mat (and plastic) out of the way and keep rolling forwards into a tight cylinder, with steady, gentle pressure.</p>",
   "heat": null,
   "id": "step-9",
   "images": {
    "alt": "Roll forwards",
    "diagram": null,
    "how": [
     {
      "caption": "Lift the mat edge out of the way and keep rolling forwards.",
      "src": "illustrations/tuna-mango-roll/9-how1.webp"
     }
    ],
    "illustration": null,
    "photo": null,
    "result": "illustrations/tuna-mango-roll/9.webp",
    "svg_fallback": null
   },
   "n": 9,
   "part": null,
   "part_id": null,
   "time": "20 s",
   "time_html": "<span>20 s</span>",
   "title": "Roll forwards",
   "uses_rows": []
  },
  {
   "body_html": "<ul class=\"do\"><li>Lay the mat over the roll and squeeze gently along its length to set the shape.</li><li>Make the second roll the same way.</li></ul>",
   "heat": null,
   "id": "step-10",
   "images": {
    "alt": "Squeeze to set",
    "diagram": null,
    "how": [
     {
      "caption": "Mat over the roll: squeeze gently along its length.",
      "src": "illustrations/tuna-mango-roll/10-how1.webp"
     }
    ],
    "illustration": null,
    "photo": null,
    "result": "illustrations/tuna-mango-roll/10.webp",
    "svg_fallback": null
   },
   "n": 10,
   "part": null,
   "part_id": null,
   "time": "10 s",
   "time_html": "<span>10 s</span>",
   "title": "Squeeze to set",
   "uses_rows": []
  },
  {
   "body_html": "<ul class=\"do\"><li>Wipe a very sharp knife with a damp cloth.</li><li>Cut the roll in half, each half in half, then each piece in half again — 8 pieces.</li><li>Wipe the blade every cut or two. Cutting through the plastic wrap keeps the rice off your fingers.</li></ul>",
   "heat": null,
   "id": "step-11",
   "images": {
    "alt": "Cut into 8",
    "diagram": null,
    "how": [
     {
      "caption": "Wipe the knife with a damp cloth before cutting.",
      "src": "illustrations/tuna-mango-roll/11-how1.webp"
     },
     {
      "caption": "Half, then quarters, then eighths.",
      "src": "illustrations/tuna-mango-roll/11-how2.webp"
     }
    ],
